  "changes": [
    "Reuse the exact vector polynomial for reference-fold target attention. Q4T uses a different double-exponential contract, which remains unchanged. No claim that polynomial reuse accelerates Q4T.",
    "Project only proposed rows without observers; retain complete observed projection and normal adapter dispatch. Anchor activations remain in all decoder layers.",
    "Distribute equal row ranges, subdivide inside each worker into bounded 128-row tiles, retain exact product/add order and per-worker errors.",
    "Use bounded 512-row product tiles when only greedy IDs are required; avoid full correction-buffer writes and preserve global tie IDs, clipping and finite checks. Full output/observer paths remain.",
    "Return one inverse per query/head, multiply each probability in binary32 immediately before widening for value accumulation, preserve exponentials, sink term and chronological sums.",
    "Resolve session metadata once per active physical expert after all metadata admission/eviction, then publish immutable views to workers. Weights and physical cache keys remain shared.",
    "For exactly seven native, unpaired Q5_K vectors, reuse the existing eight-vector arithmetic with the eighth address repeating the seventh mapped input; store only the seven live outputs. No new SIMD arithmetic, weight layout or public API.",
    "Exact CPU SIMD SiTU: port the existing Vulkan scalar-reference tanhf/expm1f/expf arithmetic into sixteen-lane CPU loops. Preserve binary32 stages, sigmoid cutoff, scalar fallback, non-finite propagation and peak tracking. Keep the existing IQ3_S/Q4T and seven-vector Q5_K projection.",
    "For native IQ3_S reference products with seven/eight queries, decode each block once for eight live accumulators instead of four at a time. Retain native110-byte blocks, original FP32 lane FMAs and sequential binary64 fold. Repeat the last input for one unused lane of seven-query calls and write only live results. Indexed input/result rows are validated before writes. Other query counts keep prior kernels.",
    "Native IQ3_S one-to-four-query kernels decode only live queries, process a validated row range in one call, preserve FP32 lane FMAs and sequential binary64 fold, and write mapped outputs directly. Existing seven/eight-query arithmetic, unsupported-count fallbacks, native 110-byte weights and guards remain.",
    "Inkling reference MoE sums weighted expert rows in rank order using separate binary32 multiplication/addition. Four output vectors remain in registers through the reduction; raw expert scratch is read only and output tiles are stored once. Original primitives handle short tails and unsupported hosts. Other architectures retain their existing reduction loop.",
    "Native five/six-query IQ3_S kernels decode once for every live query, preserve original integer lanes/FP32 FMAs and chronological binary64 folds, and write mapped outputs directly. Counts1..4 and7/8 remain supported.",
    "Native nine-to-sixteen-query IQ3_S kernel, with original scheduler/attention and matched original decoder profiles. Exact original lane/FMA/fold semantics; no repacking or extra weight cache.",
    "Reference convolution owns channels per existing CPU worker; each channel retains sequential tokens and exact tap/FMA ordering. Only False is published to an atomic finite flag; caller resolves errors/cancellation after all shares settle. Serial/small and existing non-reference SIMD paths remain. No added persistent buffers, runtime or weight expansion."
  ],
